BT /F1 10.50 Tf 54.00 488.00 Td (The relic system is data-driven. RelicLibrary reads Resources/relics.json, converts each JSON) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.50 Tf 54.00 474.50 Td (object into a RelicDefinition, and creates runtime Relic objects from those definitions. A relic) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.50 Tf 54.00 461.00 Td (does not hard-code its behavior directly. Instead, RelicFactory builds one trigger object and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.50 Tf 54.00 447.50 Td (one effect object from the trigger and effect type strings in the JSON.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.50 Tf 54.00 426.00 Td (Triggers are responsible for listening to gameplay events on EventBus. For example, the damage) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.50 Tf 54.00 412.50 Td (relic listens for OnPlayerDamaged, the kill relic listens for OnEnemyKilled, and the movement) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.50 Tf 54.00 399.00 Td (relic listens for OnPlayerMoved. When a trigger condition is satisfied, it calls) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.50 Tf 54.00 385.50 Td (Relic.Trigger\(\), which applies the relic effect to the owning PlayerController. Effects remain) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.50 Tf 54.00 372.00 Td (separate from triggers, so the same effect type can be reused by different conditions.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.50 Tf 54.00 350.50 Td (Temporary effects are handled by the effect object that created them. GainSpellPowerRelicEffect) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.50 Tf 54.00 337.00 Td (can add temporary spell power and remove it when a later event occurs, such as movement or the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.50 Tf 54.00 323.50 Td (next spell cast. Immediate effects, such as gaining mana or increasing max health, apply once) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.50 Tf 54.00 310.00 Td (and then report that they are not active.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.50 Tf 54.00 288.50 Td (Relic rewards are integrated into the existing wave reward flow. RewardScreenManager offers) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.50 Tf 54.00 275.00 Td (relics after every third wave, asks PlayerController.BuildRelicRewardChoices\(\) for three non-) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.50 Tf 54.00 261.50 Td (duplicate options, and stores those choices in GameManager. When the player advances to the next) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.50 Tf 54.00 248.00 Td (wave, EnemySpawner.NextWave\(\) gives the selected relic to the player and activates it.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.50 Tf 54.00 234.50 Td (RelicUIManager listens for relic pickup and clear events so the HUD stays synchronized with the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.50 Tf 54.00 221.00 Td (player's relic list.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.50 Tf 54.00 199.50 Td (Character classes are also data-driven. EnemySpawner reads the class names from classes.json and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.50 Tf 54.00 186.00 Td (adds class buttons to the start menu. The selected class is copied to PlayerController when a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.50 Tf 54.00 172.50 Td (level starts. PlayerController.ApplyWaveStats\(\) reevaluates health, mana, mana regeneration,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.50 Tf 54.00 159.00 Td (spell power, and speed each wave using the class RPN expressions and the current wave number.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.50 Tf 54.00 145.50 Td (Health and mana preserve their current percentage when maximum values change.) Tj ET
BT /F2 14.00 Tf 54.00 116.00 Td (Added Relics) Tj ET
